  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "اَلْحَسَنُ بْنُ مَحْبُوبٍ عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ رِئَابٍ عَنِ اِبْنِ بُكَيْرٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ عَنْ أَحَدِهِمَا عَلَيْهِمَا اَلسَّلاَمُ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub from Ali ibn Ri'ab from Ibn Bukayr from his father from one of the Imams (peace be upon them both)"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "فِي خَصِيٍّ دَلَّسَ نَفْسَهُ لِاِمْرَأَةٍ مُسْلِمَةٍ فَتَزَوَّجَهَا قَالَ «يُفَرَّقُ بَيْنَهُمَا إِنْ شَاءَتْ وَ يُوجَعُ رَأْسُهُ فَإِنْ رَضِيَتْ وَ أَقَامَتْ مَعَهُ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهَا بَعْدَ رِضَاهَا بِهِ أَنْ تَأْبَاهُ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Regarding a eunuch who concealed his condition from a Muslim woman and married her, he said: 'They are separated if she wishes, and his head is struck (with the cane). If she is pleased and stays with him, she cannot refuse him after her pleasure with him.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith outlines the legal ruling for a marriage where a eunuch concealed his condition from the bride. It establishes that the wife has the option of khula' (separation) and that a physical punishment (striking the head) is administered to the husband. If she chooses to remain, the marriage becomes binding and she cannot later demand separation.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling if a eunuch marries a woman without disclosing his condition?",
